# Ready-to-run calls for every endpoint.
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and Visual Studio 2022 (17.12+) / Rider .http support.
# Prerequisites: database running, data seeded, API running (see README).
# Run the requests top to bottom: later requests reuse ids / RowVersions from earlier responses (# @name).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5010
@userName = dana.cohen

### Health check (200 Healthy)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### List – default (page 1, 20 per page, newest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets

### List – combined filters, sorting and paging
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets?status=New&status=Waiting&priority=High&createdFrom=2026-01-01&createdTo=2026-06-30T23:59:59Z&sortBy=priority&sortDir=asc&page=2&pageSize=10

### List – filter by assignee and organization
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets?assignedTo=dana.cohen&organizationName=Acme%20Logistics&sortBy=updatedAt

### List – prefix search on Title or OrganizationName (works in Hebrew too)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets?search=Invoice&sortBy=title&sortDir=asc

### List – invalid query → 400 ValidationProblemDetails (pageSize, sortBy, createdTo)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets?pageSize=1000&sortBy=id&createdFrom=2026-02-01&createdTo=2026-01-01

### Summary (cached up to 60 s, invalidated after every committed status change)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/summary

### Pick two "New" tickets to work with (ids and RowVersions are reused below)
# @name newTickets
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets?status=New&pageSize=2&sortBy=createdAt&sortDir=asc

@ticketId = {{newTickets.response.body.$.items[0].id}}
@originalRowVersion = {{newTickets.response.body.$.items[0].rowVersion}}
@secondTicketId = {{newTickets.response.body.$.items[1].id}}
@secondRowVersion = {{newTickets.response.body.$.items[1].rowVersion}}

### Single ticket (includes the current RowVersion)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{ticketId}}

### Status update – New → InProgress (200, returns the NEW RowVersion)
# @name update
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{ticketId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Name: {{userName}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-update-1

{
  "newStatus": "InProgress",
  "rowVersion": "{{originalRowVersion}}"
}

### Concurrency conflict – same request again with the OLD RowVersion → 409 with currentTicket
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{ticketId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Name: other.user

{
  "newStatus": "Waiting",
  "rowVersion": "{{originalRowVersion}}"
}

### Invalid transition – InProgress → New → 422 with allowedStatuses
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{ticketId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newStatus": "New",
  "rowVersion": "{{update.response.body.$.rowVersion}}"
}

### Unknown ticket → 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/999999/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newStatus": "InProgress",
  "rowVersion": "AAAAAAAAAAE="
}

### Malformed body → 400 (newStatus, rowVersion)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{ticketId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### History of the updated ticket (newest first; ChangedBy and CorrelationId from the update above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{ticketId}}/history

### Bulk – partial success: one Updated (New → InProgress), one Conflict (outdated RowVersion), one NotFound
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/bulk-status
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Name: {{userName}}

{
  "newStatus": "InProgress",
  "items": [
    { "id": {{secondTicketId}}, "rowVersion": "{{secondRowVersion}}" },
    { "id": {{ticketId}}, "rowVersion": "{{originalRowVersion}}" },
    { "id": 999999, "rowVersion": "AAAAAAAAAAE=" }
  ]
}

### Bulk – invalid request (duplicate ids) → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/bulk-status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newStatus": "Waiting",
  "items": [
    { "id": 1, "rowVersion": "AAAAAAAAAAE=" },
    { "id": 1, "rowVersion": "AAAAAAAAAAE=" }
  ]
}
